Manager Sustainability
ACI EUROPE - Airports Council International
Brussels, Belgium
ACI EUROPE is hiring a Manager Sustainability responsible for Sustainable Aviation Fuels (SAF), new energy aircraft, airport electrification & energy infrastructure, aircraft noise management, circular economy and intermodality activities reporting to the Director of Sustainability.
SCOPE
To promote, through ACI EUROPE, the interests of around 600 European airports to legislators, regulators, the press and the public;
To provide ACI EUROPE members with high-quality information and analysis on European legislative and regulatory developments;
To contribute to the formulation of ACI EUROPE policy, including initiating and coordinating the development of positions on assigned sustainability files;
To represent ACI EUROPE in European legislative and non-legislative bodies, and other international fora. Travel to be expected (approx. 25% of working time).
ESSENTIAL QUALITIES
Genuine interest in decarbonisation, including more technical aspects;
Very good understanding of the technical challenges of aviation decarbonisation;
Very good understanding of the general European and International climate policy context;
Ability to originate and produce high quality, coherent, reasoned and convincing written materials;
Ability to perform in-depth analyses, including technical and quantitative aspects;
Highly developed social and communication skills, including the ability to communicate in a multilingual and multicultural environment;
Ability to translate technical and regulatory information into practical policy input and member briefings;
Ability to work in a Team, listen to others, foster compromise and obtain consensus;
Ability to work in a fast-moving and demanding environment, including flexibility to adjust to an evolving portfolio of activities;
Fluent in English both written and spoken;
Computer literacy.
APPLICATION
ACI EUROPE offers an attractive remuneration package and benefits for the right candidate.
Please send your CV (maximum 2 pages), together with a one-page cover letter (in English) and any relevant supporting material to:
stephanie.coppin@aci-europe.org
and
philippe.sacre@aci-europe.org
.
Application deadline:
31 October 2026
www.aci-europe.org
Don't forget to mention EuroBrussels when applying.
