EU Public Affairs Intern in Energy & Mobility Policy
PI - Political Intelligence
Brussels, Belgium
€ 1.077 per month
Our Public Affairs consultancy is looking for a motivated EU Public Affairs intern to reinforce our Energy and Mobility Policy team. The internship will include assisting in the work of key client accounts, monitoring and analysis of EU political trends, EU policy research, in-depth analysis and organisational support for various clients active in the energy and mobility sectors.
If you’re ready to gain knowledge on the EU policy sphere, make an impact, and work on issues that matter – you might be the intern we’re looking for!
Main Responsibilities:
Assist in the work of key client accounts and in the organisation of events;
Follow key policies debates in the main European Institutions and report to clients;
Assist in MEP mappings, political analysis & events organisation;
Contribute to research and analysis of policy issues and legislation;
Prepare regular news reports and political analysis;
Research on various issues and write short reports;
Attend conferences, seminar, hearings and so much more!
What We’re Looking For:
Excellent level of English with any additional EU languages being an asset;
Passion for EU policies with a solid understanding of the EU, its institutions and policy-making processes;
A university level degree in a relevant field;
Strong analytical skills and the ability to interpret and analyse legislation, political developments, rules and regulations and summarise them in a clear and concise manner;
An eye for detail and the ability manage effectively your time and priorities;
Demonstration of assertiveness, flexibility and autonomy;
Team player with good communication and inter-personal skills.
Apply Now
