Internship in Public Affairs Team
Euroclear
Brussels, Belgium
What you will do:
You will assist and provide support to the Public Affairs team, part of the Compliance and Public Affairs Division, on a variety of topics;
Activities may include: supporting the preparation of briefing notes, presentations and materials, assisting with the monitoring of policy discussions and developments, conducting research and contributing to a variety of tasks in the team;
Be part of the team’s interactions and activities, which provide ample opportunities for development and practical learning.
What we are looking for:
You have an active student status (Bachelor) or (Master) in one or more of the following areas: Finance, Banking and Financial Law, European politics, International Relations and related subjects. A strong interest in financial markets is essential to make the most of the role. Technology and European politics are also relevant areas in our work;
You have an excellent level of English, including drafting and communication skills. Knowledge of a second/third language is a plus;
You are a team player but are also able to work autonomously;
You have strong analytical and research skills;
You are discrete, well organized and stress resistant.
