Senior Public Affairs Professional
#SustainablePublicAffairs
Brussels, Belgium
#SustainablePublicAffairs is looking for a senior public affairs professional to join its young and bright team and advice sustainable frontrunner clients that want to make an ambitious, positive impact on EU policies.
The ideal candidate embraces #SustainablePublicAffairs’ mission to make the practices of sustainable frontrunners the norm for the rest of their industry.
This means you are a proactive, big-picture thinker, not afraid to have an opinion, and encourage your team members to express their views. You are able to offer creative solutions to complex issues while contributing to the growth of this young, fast-growing organisation. You enjoy contributing to the organisation and developing a team.
Your personal growth is only limited by yourself: we encourage a lot of autonomy to develop our existing portfolio of frontrunner clients but also broaden it, and we count on your out-of-the-box thinking and entrepreneurial spirit to make your client’s narratives stand out from the crowd.
YOUR ROLE AND RESPONSIBILITIES
Client and Advisory:
Provide strategic advice on EU public and regulatory affairs to a portfolio of sustainable frontrunner clients;
Manage accounts and client relationships, including:
Managing day-to-day operations and work programmes independently; act as main point of contact for clients;
Anticipating and understanding what the client needs and translating this into unique strategies and narratives for existing and new EU policy files;
Developing and implementing impactful EU public affairs strategies, performing regular fitness checks, identifying threats and opportunities and how best to respond;
Providing supporting analysis for the drafting of position papers, briefings, speeches and presentations.
Develop a good knowledge of current policy developments and how they are affecting our clients’ business;
Establish a strong network with policymakers, industry/trade associations, media, and others to raise the profile of clients’ issues and solutions;
Think outside of the box and propose creative solutions to ensure client objectives are reached;
Think ahead: consider longer-term outlook on potential future workstreams and resources.
People Management:
Mentor colleagues working on your client team in terms of content and deliverables, ensuring they have the skills they need to deliver quality work;
Be the go-to person for team members to advise on day-to-day responsibilities and broader professional development;
Safeguard the general wellbeing of colleagues, actively propose ideas to improve teamwork.
Support broader #SustainablePublicAffairs activities:
Be a well-known name in your network for content expertise and expand this network through e.g. public speaking, publishing thought-leadership pieces, moderating events;
