ABOUT YOU
You are impact and values driven, able to see the big picture whilst taking care of the details. You have experience in EU policy-making processes and are a good networker. You are a team player who can also play solo. You thrive when facing complex situations, you are passionate about the zero waste vision and well aware of the multiple challenges the world is facing today.
ABOUT THE ROLE
The Zero Pollution Policy Manager advances EU policies to prevent pollution and support the transition towards a circular economy. The role takes a holistic approach to addressing waste generation and its climate and environmental impacts, focusing on residual waste, biowaste, food waste, and bioplastics. It promotes waste prevention and reduction, sustainable material management and recovery, and policies that address the underlying causes of waste generation.
This includes advocating for:
Residual waste reduction targets and cap-and-trade systems;
Alternatives to incineration such as Material Recovery and Biological Treatment, and avoiding simply shifting waste from landfilling to incineration without addressing the underlying causes of waste generation;
Sustainable biowaste and food waste management policies;
Safeguards around bioplastics that contribute to circularity and pollution prevention.
Across these interconnected topics, the role seeks to prevent the shifting of environmental impacts between waste management options and to advance coherent EU policies that deliver genuine pollution reduction and systemic change, in collaboration with other teams at Zero Waste Europe.
CORE RESPONSIBILITIES
Policy development and advocacy:
Develop and implement EU policy and advocacy strategies to address the above mentioned topics, connecting climate and circular economy objectives;
Monitor and influence EU policy developments and legislation, developing evidence-based recommendations on residual waste reduction, material recovery, sustainable residual waste management, biowaste, foodwaste and alternative feedstocks;
Promote integrated policy approaches and instruments that reduce the generation of mixed waste, maximise material recovery and avoid shifting waste from landfilling to incineration, including residual waste targets, cap-and-trade systems and Material Recovery and Biological Treatment (MRBT);
Collaborate across ZWE teams to ensure a coherent approach to waste, climate and circular economy policies.
Stakeholder engagement and coalition building:
Engage with EU institutions, policymakers and other stakeholders to advance policy recommendations and build support for more circular, climate-friendly waste management systems;
Identify synergies between EU and local policy work, coordinate with ZWE members, partners and coalitions to develop joint positions, share expertise and strengthen collective advocacy;
Support ZWE members by organising and/or leading on capacity building activities. Ensuring coordination with members when undertaking advocacy activities, for maximum impact.
Communications and external representation:
Represent ZWE at public events, policy negotiations and in the media, adapting key messages to different audiences and promoting the organisation’s broader priorities.
Strategy, project management and fundraising:
Actively contribute to the policy team’s strategy, identifying and developing new areas of focus and work opportunities;
Lead on specific campaigns and projects, ensuring effective cross-team collaboration and proper follow-up;
Identify and secure funding opportunities for your area of work, develop strong donor relationships and proposals, manage project budgets and reporting, and contribute to the policy team’s fundraising strategy;
Contribute to fundraising and donor reporting to support the development and implementation of ZWE's wider policy and advocacy work.
This is a non-exclusive list, and more tasks may be required as the organisation evolves and the selected candidate grows in their role.
REQUIRED SKILLS AND COMPETENCIES
At least 5 years of experience in a senior EU policy making role;
Proven experience in fundraising, donor relations and grants management;
Experience in leading advocacy efforts and creating networks of influence;
Experienced in interacting with EU and national policymakers’ and industry professionals;
Proficient in the English language;
