Senior Rewards and Employment Officer
ESM - European Stability Mechanism
Luxembourg
Job description
Deadline for application:
20 December 2026.
We are looking for a Senior Rewards and Employment Officer to join the Human Resources and Organisation (HR) division. The role requires strong compensation and benefits expertise, analytical rigour, and sound judgement to develop evidence-based recommendations that help the ESM attract and retain talent, as well as to ensure internal equity and financial sustainability. The responsibilities span HR budgeting and forecasting, remuneration and allowance reviews, retirement and insurance arrangements, governance reporting, and the implementation of approved changes. By working closely with the Finance & Control division and other internal stakeholders, you will translate complex HR and financial information into clear advice and practical solutions. While you will report to the Head of HR and Organisation, your day-to-day supervision and work prioritisation will be provided by the Rewards and Employment Team Lead. Within this framework, you will take technical ownership of assigned workstreams, coordinate delivery with colleagues, and escalate matters requiring guidance or approval. At the ESM, this role is best suited to a collaborative professional who is as invested in the success and development of the team as in their own.
Key Accountabilities
Develop HR budget inputs, staff-cost projections, overall budget forecasts, and scenario analyses in close cooperation with the Finance & Control division and other relevant stakeholders. Assess the financial impact of headcount and policy changes, monitor expenditures, analyse variances, and prepare budget reporting and explanatory material;
Review staff compensation, allowances, and benefits (including post-employment benefits), focusing on eligibility criteria, calculation methods, and administration processes. Develop evidence-based costed recommendations, setting out options, risks, and implementation implications for decision-making;
Conduct market benchmarking and analyse salary structures, salary positioning, and remuneration outcomes to assess competitiveness, support consistent application of the reward framework, and identify potential internal equity issues;
Coordinate annual salary review and performance award processes, including the analysis and administration of promotion and salary adjustment requests, ensuring accurate calculations, appropriate documentation, and timely delivery;
Review rewards and employment policies, procedures, and processes to develop proposals for amendments to relevant internal rules. Provide technical advice on complex compensation, benefits, and allowance matters, ensuring consistent interpretation and escalating exceptions through the appropriate channels;
Prepare clear, decision-ready notes, presentations, and speaking points for HR and remuneration governance processes, including for the ESM Board of Directors, Budget Review and Compensation Committee, and Retirement Plan Committee;
Contribute to the review and administration of retirement, insurance, and post-employment benefit arrangements, analysing provider information, costs, and implementation requirements and coordinating follow-up with relevant stakeholders;
Contribute to procurement processes, provider selection and contract reviews, for Rewards and Employment team services. Monitor delivery against agreed requirements and coordinate the resolution of operational issues with providers and internal stakeholders;
Deliver assigned HR project workstreams, managing milestones, dependencies, and stakeholder coordination. Translate approved changes into implementation plans, operational procedures, and clear staff and manager communications;
Maintain and strengthen controls and documentation for compensation, benefits, and payroll-related processes. Support the review and verification of monthly payroll, ensure consistency with applicable internal rules, and contribute to audit reviews and follow-up actions;
Develop and maintain key performance indicators, dashboards, and management reporting for HR budget and reward activities. Ensure data quality, consistency, and reconciliation across HR, payroll, and financial systems, provide functional expertise on HR systems and databases, and translate data into actionable insights;
Identify and implement proportionate improvements to reward processes and reporting, including suitable automation solutions, in coordination other stakeholders and with appropriate safeguards for confidentiality, data protection, and human oversight;
Collaborate with HR team members, management, and colleagues within the organisation on HR-related matters;
Represent the ESM in international forums and exchange with peers in financial institutions to gain insight on organisational needs, exchange relevant benchmarking information, and strengthen the ESM’s employee value proposition and inclusive workplace. Share technical knowledge and support team continuity and collective delivery beyond own area of expertise.
Key Background & Experience
Advanced university degree or equivalent, preferably with a specialisation in human resource management, finance, business administration, or accounting;
At least eight years of relevant professional experience, including substantial hands-on experience in compensation and benefits analysis, reward policy development and implementation, and delivery of complex reward projects;
Demonstrated experience in HR or staff-cost budgeting, financial forecasting, scenario modelling and management reporting, including assessment of the financial impact of policy changes and close cooperation with finance and accounting teams;
Strong practical knowledge of compensation and benefits methodologies, including market benchmarking, salary structures, salary positioning, internal equity analysis, and allowance reviews, with experience developing costed recommendations and supporting remuneration governance;
Experience interpreting complex policies or internal rules and translating them into consistent operational procedures and well-documented advice. Familiarity with retirement, insurance, and post-employment benefit arrangements, and related provider or contract management, would be an asset;
Experience working in an international and multicultural environment; experience in an international organisation would be an asset;
Experience improving processes and reporting through digital tools and automation; familiarity with the responsible use of artificial intelligence-enabled solutions would be an asset;
Proven expertise in HR systems and databases, notably Oracle HCM, data quality controls and reconciliation, key performance indicators, dashboards, and management reporting. Advanced proficiency in Excel and experience with business intelligence and data analysis tools, notably Power BI, with the ability to turn complex HR and financial data into clear insights;
Demonstrated ability to prepare concise governance papers and explain technical reward and financial matters to senior stakeholders and non-specialised audiences;
Experience delivering defined project workstreams and coordinating milestones, dependencies, and implementation with HR, finance, legal, and information technology teams, as well as with and external providers, as relevant;
Excellent oral and written English skills; other language skills would be an asset.
Key Competencies
Problem solving, analytical, and numerical skills;
Critical thinking and sound judgement;
Attention to detail;
Teamwork and collaboration;
Communication and interpersonal skills;
Resilience and flexibility;
Organisation and prioritisation skills;
Learning agility.
