Keep the team moving by helping with planning, scheduling, meeting prep, notes and follow-up on actions;
Connect with colleagues across the business to gather input, share updates and keep everyone in the loop on Public Affairs activity;
Contribute to campaigns, events, presentations and position papers, and support our external partners and agencies.
What You’ll Have
You’re enrolled in a Bachelor’s or Master’s programme for the duration of the internship, for example Political Science, Public Administration, European Studies, International Relations, Communications or a related field;
You bring a strong interest in politics, public policy and societal issues, especially those affecting cities, housing, tourism and hospitality;
You’re proactive, curious and analytically sharp;
You can distil complex information into clear, concise summaries and you write well;
